      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is it really easier to learn in an automatic in York?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Generally, yes. York's stop-start traffic, especially around the busy city walls and the Barbican, can be highly taxing in a manual. Choosing automatic driving lessons in York completely removes the need for constant clutch control, allowing you to focus on the busy surroundings."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I drive a manual car if I pass in an automatic?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. If you pass your test in an automatic, your licence will be restricted to automatic vehicles only. If you want to drive a manual later, you'll need to take another practical test after preparing with a manual driving instructor in York."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are automatic lessons more expensive in York?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Slightly. Automatic cars are generally more expensive to buy and maintain, which is reflected in the hourly rate. However, many students find they need far fewer lessons to reach test standard, which can actually reduce the total cost of passing your driving test first time in York."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which is better for a nervous learner?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Automatic is typically the preferred choice for those who feel anxious about driving. Removing the risk of stalling and the complexity of gear changes significantly reduces the 'mental load' when learning on busy roads like Gillygate, helping you overcome driving test nerves."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Will I find it hard to buy an automatic car in York?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not at all. The rapid shift towards electric and hybrid vehicles means that more and more cars on the market are automatic. You'll have plenty of high-quality options at local dealerships."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a manual licence better for job opportunities?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For certain specific roles, like driving commercial vans, heavy trades, or certain utility vehicles, a manual licence is still required. However, many modern company car fleets are now switching fully to automatic or electric vehicles."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does passing in an automatic affect my insurance in York?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It can sometimes be slightly higher, as automatic gearboxes can be more expensive to resolve physically. However, factors like your age, where you live in York (like YO10 vs YO24), and your driving history will have a much bigger impact."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I switch from manual to automatic lessons?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Absolutely. Many students start in a manual and find it's not for them. Switching to automatic can often be the breakthrough they need to start enjoying their lessons and making real progress."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does it take to learn the gears in a manual?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It varies, but it usually takes several hours of dedicated practice to get the 'feel' for the clutch on your manual driving lessons in York. In an automatic, you can usually get comfortable with the basic controls in the first 20 minutes."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are automatic cars less safe on the York bypass?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No, they are just as safe. In fact, many people feel safer because they don't have to worry about being in the wrong gear when merging onto fast-moving roads, which is a key part of preparing for York driving test routes."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is fuel consumption different between automatic and manual?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "In older cars, manuals were more efficient. However, modern automatic gearboxes are incredibly advanced and often match or even beat manuals for fuel economy."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you offer intensive courses for both?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, we do. Whether you choose automatic or manual, our intensive driving courses in York are designed to help you progress quickly and get to that test-ready standard in a shorter timeframe."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What if I change my mind after my first lesson?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "That's why we recommend a standard first lesson to see how you feel. We'll give you honest feedback on which path we think would suit your learning style and goals best, and we can also prepare mock driving tests in York once you reach standard."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are electric cars always automatic?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, almost all electric vehicles (EVs) are automatic. If you're planning on buying an electric car in the future, learning in an automatic is a very sensible long-term choice."
